From: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zebra: let a dataplane module learn local MACs

In SONiC's FPM MAC sync mode (FDB_SYNC mac_sync_mode fpm), zebra runs
with --kernel-mac-ext-learn and loads dplane_fpm_sonic, the dataplane
plugin that talks FPM to fpmsyncd. The ASIC learns local MACs, fpmsyncd
reports them over the FPM channel, and dplane_fpm_sonic keeps them,
hands them to zebra and writes their kernel bridge FDB entries. So in
this mode the kernel is not a source of local MACs, and zebra must not
learn them from it. zebra still creates a MAC for an ARP/ND entry (an
auto MAC); when dplane_fpm_sonic reports the MAC, it becomes a local
MAC, as it does on a kernel learn.

The local MACs the kernel reports are zebra's own writes. Patch 0033
drops them by NDA_PROTOCOL, which works while the kernel keeps a
protocol for bridge FDB entries: SONiC's kernel patch
0002-net-bridge-vxlan-Protocol-field-in-bridge-fdb.patch adds it, and
sonic-net/sonic-linux-kernel#619 removes that patch, as nothing needs
protocol-scoped FDB entries once MACs are synced over FPM. Without it,
the bridge reports zebra's write with no protocol, and zebra takes it
for a local learn: for a host the Ethernet Segment peer advertises but
this switch has not seen, the MAC turns active, is advertised as learnt
here, and stays after the peer withdraws it.

This patch adds zebra_neigh_set_dplane_mac_learning(), which
dplane_fpm_sonic calls when zebra runs in mac-ext-learn mode. While it
is set:

- zebra ignores the kernel's bridge FDB messages (RTM_NEWNEIGH and
  RTM_DELNEIGH, AF_BRIDGE) for local ports, adds and deletes alike.
  Those for the VXLAN device concern remote MACs and are processed as
  before.

- zebra drops a local MAC for a VLAN with no L2VNI, and gets the local
  MACs of a VLAN again from a read of the kernel bridge FDB when an
  L2VNI is added or comes up, and when BGP enables advertise-all-vni.
  The read's local entries are ignored as above, so after it zebra now
  calls the new zebra_dplane_mac_read hook, and dplane_fpm_sonic hands
  zebra the MACs it keeps.

- When the peer-active hold timer of a MAC expires, mac-ext-learn mode
  flushes the MAC, as no dynamic learn happens while it is static
  (patch 0034). That stays for a local-inactive MAC. An active MAC is
  one the ASIC learnt itself, for instance from a host whose traffic
  reached this switch before the peer advertised it: the ASIC ages it,
  and fpmsyncd reports when it does, so flushing it only withdraws the
  route of a host still behind this switch, until dplane_fpm_sonic
  gives the MAC back. Such a MAC now just loses peer-active, as without
  mac-ext-learn.

- dplane_fpm_sonic installs a sync MAC (a host the Ethernet Segment
  peer advertises) in the ASIC as a static entry when zebra writes the
  MAC as static, and removes it when zebra writes the MAC as a normal
  entry or deletes it. mac-ext-learn mode writes a local MAC only while
  it is local-inactive, so when an active MAC with such an entry stopped
  being static, at hold timer expiry or when its last synced neighbour
  was deleted, zebra wrote nothing, and the static entry stayed in the
  ASIC, where it does not age. zebra now writes such a MAC once more as
  a normal entry.

Signed-off-by: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
---
diff --git a/zebra/zebra_evpn.c b/zebra/zebra_evpn.c
index 945ec8541f..2209e94d5b 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_evpn.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_evpn.c
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@
 #include "zebra/zebra_dplane.h"
 #include "zebra/zebra_router.h"
 #include "zebra/zebra_trace.h"
+#include "zebra/zebra_neigh.h"
 
 DEFINE_MTYPE_STATIC(ZEBRA, ZEVPN, "VNI hash");
 DEFINE_MTYPE_STATIC(ZEBRA, ZEVPN_VTEP, "VNI remote VTEP");
@@ -953,6 +954,10 @@ void zebra_evpn_read_mac_neigh(struct zebra_evpn *zevpn, struct interface *ifp)
 			zif->brslave_info.bridge_ifindex);
 
 	dplane_fdb_read_for_bridge(zns, ifp, zif->brslave_info.br_if, vni->access_vlan);
+	/* The local MACs this read reports are ignored while a dataplane
+	 * module learns them, so ask the module instead.
+	 */
+	zebra_neigh_dplane_mac_read(zevpn);
 	/* We need to specifically read and retrieve the entry for BUM handling
 	 * via multicast, if any.
 	 */
diff --git a/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c b/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c
index 5f9f84f34e..f98d664bda 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include "zebra/zebra_evpn_mh.h"
 #include "zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.h"
 #include "zebra/zebra_evpn_neigh.h"
+#include "zebra/zebra_neigh.h"
 
 DEFINE_MTYPE_STATIC(ZEBRA, MAC, "EVPN MAC");
 
@@ -1480,9 +1481,13 @@ int zebra_evpn_sync_mac_dp_install(struct zebra_mac *mac, bool set_inactive,
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	if (!zebra_mac_ext_learn_mode() || CHECK_FLAG(mac->flags, ZEBRA_MAC_LOCAL_INACTIVE)) {
+	if (!zebra_mac_ext_learn_mode() || CHECK_FLAG(mac->flags, ZEBRA_MAC_LOCAL_INACTIVE) ||
+	    (zebra_neigh_dplane_mac_learning() && !set_static)) {
 		/* For Extern Only mode:
-		 *  Update the dataplane only when the MAC is inactive
+		 *  Update the dataplane only when the MAC is inactive, or when
+		 *  an active MAC stops being static and a dataplane module
+		 *  learns local MACs: the module keeps the static entry in
+		 *  the ASIC until this write ends it.
 		 */
 		if (IS_ZEBRA_DEBUG_EVPN_MH_MAC) {
 			char mac_buf[MAC_BUF_SIZE];
@@ -1546,7 +1551,13 @@ static void zebra_evpn_mac_hold_exp_cb(struct event *t)
 			   zebra_evpn_zebra_mac_flag_dump(mac, mac_buf, sizeof(mac_buf)));
 	}
 
-	if (zebra_mac_ext_learn_mode()) {
+	/* A dataplane module that learns local MACs also ages them, so only a
+	 * local-inactive MAC is flushed here; an active one stays until the
+	 * module reports it gone.
+	 */
+	if (zebra_mac_ext_learn_mode() &&
+	    (!zebra_neigh_dplane_mac_learning() ||
+	     CHECK_FLAG(mac->flags, ZEBRA_MAC_LOCAL_INACTIVE))) {
 		vlanid_t vid;
 		struct interface *ifp;
 		/* Upon expiry, MAC is deleted from DP. */
diff --git a/zebra/zebra_neigh.c b/zebra/zebra_neigh.c
index b0350e2c0d..3c37e3ee59 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_neigh.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_neigh.c
@@ -580,6 +580,26 @@ static void zebra_neigh_ipaddr_update(struct zebra_dplane_ctx *ctx)
 		zebra_vxlan_handle_kernel_neigh_del(ifp, link_if, &ip);
 }
 
+static bool dplane_mac_learning;
+
+DEFINE_HOOK(zebra_dplane_mac_read, (struct zebra_evpn *zevpn), (zevpn));
+
+void zebra_neigh_set_dplane_mac_learning(bool enable)
+{
+	dplane_mac_learning = enable;
+}
+
+bool zebra_neigh_dplane_mac_learning(void)
+{
+	return dplane_mac_learning;
+}
+
+void zebra_neigh_dplane_mac_read(struct zebra_evpn *zevpn)
+{
+	if (dplane_mac_learning)
+		hook_call(zebra_dplane_mac_read, zevpn);
+}
+
 static void zebra_neigh_macfdb_update(struct zebra_dplane_ctx *ctx)
 {
 	ns_id_t ns_id;
@@ -653,6 +673,14 @@ static void zebra_neigh_macfdb_update(struct zebra_dplane_ctx *ctx)
 	ndm_state = dplane_ctx_mac_get_ndm_state(ctx);
 	ndm_flags = dplane_ctx_mac_get_ndm_flags(ctx);
 
+	/* The dataplane module learns local MACs; this entry is zebra's own write. */
+	if (dplane_mac_learning && !IS_ZEBRA_IF_VXLAN(ifp)) {
+		if (IS_ZEBRA_DEBUG_KERNEL)
+			zlog_debug("        Ignoring %s MAC %pEA on %s, a dataplane module learns local MACs",
+				   dplane_op2str(op), &mac, ifp->name);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/* If add or update, do accordingly if learnt on a "local" interface; if
 	 * the notification is over VxLAN, this has to be related to
 	 * multi-homing,
diff --git a/zebra/zebra_neigh.h b/zebra/zebra_neigh.h
index 30c9f4b644..086a1888fb 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_neigh.h
+++ b/zebra/zebra_neigh.h
@@ -14,12 +14,15 @@
 #include "lib/prefix.h"
 #include "lib/ns.h"
 #include "lib/if.h"
+#include "lib/hook.h"
 
 struct zebra_pbr_rule;
 struct zebra_dplane_ctx;
 
 #define zneigh_info zrouter.neigh_info
 
+struct zebra_evpn;
+
 struct zebra_neigh_ent {
 	ns_id_t ns_id;
 	ifindex_t ifindex;
@@ -60,4 +63,12 @@ extern void zebra_neigh_deref(struct zebra_pbr_rule *rule);
 extern void zebra_neigh_ref(ns_id_t ns_id, int ifindex, struct ipaddr *ip,
 			    struct zebra_pbr_rule *rule);
 void zebra_neigh_dplane_update(struct zebra_dplane_ctx *ctx);
+/* A dataplane module, not the kernel, learns and ages local MACs. */
+extern void zebra_neigh_set_dplane_mac_learning(bool enable);
+extern bool zebra_neigh_dplane_mac_learning(void);
+/* Where zebra reads local MACs from the kernel, it asks that module for them
+ * instead. zevpn is the EVPN being read, or NULL for all of them.
+ */
+DECLARE_HOOK(zebra_dplane_mac_read, (struct zebra_evpn *zevpn), (zevpn));
+extern void zebra_neigh_dplane_mac_read(struct zebra_evpn *zevpn);
 #endif /* _ZEBRA_NEIGH_H */
diff --git a/zebra/zebra_vxlan.c b/zebra/zebra_vxlan.c
index 42ed7e1ea8..26732fac2c 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_vxlan.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_vxlan.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 #include "zebra/zebra_dplane.h"
 #include "zebra/zebra_router.h"
 #include "zebra/zebra_trace.h"
+#include "zebra/zebra_neigh.h"
 
 DEFINE_MTYPE_STATIC(ZEBRA, HOST_PREFIX, "host prefix");
 DEFINE_MTYPE_STATIC(ZEBRA, ZL3VNI, "L3 VNI hash");
@@ -6066,6 +6067,7 @@ void zebra_vxlan_advertise_all_vni(ZAPI_HANDLER_ARGS)
 
 		/* Read the MAC FDB */
 		ns_walk_func(macfdb_read_ns, NULL, NULL);
+		zebra_neigh_dplane_mac_read(NULL);
 
 		/* Read neighbors */
 		ns_walk_func(neigh_read_ns, NULL, NULL);
